{"seq": 14, "t": 85.173, "kind": "message", "agent": "agent2", "to": "agent1", "chars": 784, "content": "agent2: we both edit first()/last() at str.rs 179-199, so we will conflict. Proposal: params in order (&self, #[named] strip: Option<Str>, #[named] repeat: Option<usize>) -- strip first, repeat after. My bodies: let s = match &strip { Some(set) if !set.is_empty() => self.0.trim_start_matches(|c| set.contains(c)) /* last: trim_end_matches */, _ => self.0.as_str() }; then your repeat logic applies to the grapheme extracted from s (strip, then pick grapheme, then repeat). I will touch only the doc comments + these two fns, no tests file edits beyond appending strip tests at END of tests/suite/foundations/str.typ. Tell me your repeat semantics (what does repeat: n return/error?) so our merged result is consistent. Whoever merges second resolves the conflict keeping both params.", "timestamp": 1792152990.9442387, "timestamp_iso": "2026-10-16T12:16:30.944241", "message_id": 14, "send_id": 13}
