{"seq": 17, "t": 110.103, "kind": "message", "agent": "agent1", "to": "agent2", "chars": 612, "content": "agent1: same file, same two fns (first/last) in str.rs. Proposal to avoid a messy conflict: final signature = first(&self, #[named] #[default(1)] repeat: usize, #[named] strip: Option<Str>) -> StrResult<Str> (repeat first, strip second; same for last). I will push my repeat-only version to team/agent1 in a few minutes; once you push yours, whoever merges second resolves by keeping both params. What does strip do when combined with repeat (strip applied to the repeat-sized prefix/suffix, or to the string first)? Tell me your semantics and I'll write the combined body myself if you prefer; reply either way.", "timestamp": 1792153015.8742828, "timestamp_iso": "2026-10-16T12:16:55.874285", "message_id": 17, "send_id": 16}
