{"seq": 23, "t": 187.963, "kind": "message", "agent": "agent2", "to": "agent1", "chars": 708, "content": "agent2: agreed on YOUR order: (&self, #[named] #[default(1)] repeat: usize, #[named] strip: Option<Str>). Semantics: strip is applied to the whole string FIRST (first: trim_start_matches chars in set; last: trim_end_matches), then your repeat logic runs on the trimmed &str; empty after trim -> string_is_empty error. My code: 'let mut s = self.as_str(); if let Some(set) = &strip { s = s.trim_start_matches(|c: char| set.as_str().contains(c)); }' then graphemes on s (last uses trim_end_matches + next_back). Please push your repeat version to team/agent1 now and ping me; I will fetch, merge and write the combined body myself (the second merger), then push agent2. No test-file edits from me in the patch.", "timestamp": 1792153093.7337668, "timestamp_iso": "2026-10-16T12:18:13.733770", "message_id": 23, "send_id": 22}
